  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall be begun before the expiration of three years from the date of this permission.",
    "Condition : 2 - The proposed development shall be carried out in all respects in accordance with the proposals contained in the application and the plans submitted (Drawings SK2/REVB/2018, 109/ExistingFP, 109/FPPREVA/2018, 1480/1A, 1480/1AB, 1480/3C, Location Plan, Cover Letter, Eco Shelter Range specification (Urban Shelters; product ref. USP/ES12/6HR), Sustainability Assessment (dated 23rd July 2020) and Transport Assessment (dated July 2020) [received 27th July 2020]) therewith and approved by the Local Planning Authority, or as shall have been otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority before the building is used.",
    "Condition : 3 - The materials to be used in the construction of the external surfaces of the extension hereby permitted shall match those used in the existing building.",
    "Condition : 4 - During the course of the development: \r\na.\tThe Local Planning Authority shall be notified immediately if additional contamination is discovered during the course of the development. A competent person shall assess any such additional contamination, and shall submit appropriate amendments to the scheme for decontamination in writing to the Local Planning Authority for approval before any work on that aspect of development continues. These amendments shall demonstrate how the unsuspected contamination will be dealt with and set out appropriate remediation measures.\r\nBefore the development is first brought into use:\r\nb.\tThe agreed scheme for decontamination referred to in clause a) above, including amendments, shall be fully implemented and a written validation (closure) report submitted to the Local Planning Authority for approval.\r\n",
    "Condition : 5 - Before the extension hereby permitted is brought into use the cycle parking facilities shown on the approved drawings 1480/1A and 1480/1AB and Eco Shelter Range specification (Urban Shelters; product ref. USP/ES12/6HR), received 27th July 2020, shall be provided and thereafter retained as such.",
    "Condition : 6 - Prior to first occupation of the extension hereby permitted an evidence pack (including for example manufactures literature, post construction reports, photos and statements of compliance) shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority to show that the development has been constructed in accordance with the approved Sustainability Assessment (dated 23rd July 2020).",
    "Condition : 7 - No more than 225 people shall be employed at the site at any one time without the written authorisation of the Local Planning Authority.",
    "Condition : 8 - The extension hereby approved shall be used for general industrial and/or storage and distribution purposes and shall remain ancillary to the use of the building to which it would be adjoined; it shall be used for no other purposes.",
    "Condition : 9 - The existing vehicular crossover on the south-eastern elevation of the application site, adjacent to the development hereby permitted, shall be made good, and the kerb and verge/footway reinstated, at the expense of the applicant, prior to the first occupation of the hereby approved single storey rear extension."
  ],
